chapters.intro_en_source:
It has three well-known names:
Fātiḥat al-Kitāb—The Opening of the Book;
Umm al-Qurʾān—The Mother of the Qur’an;
and al-Sabʿ al-Mathānī—The Seven Oft-Repeated Verses.
It is also called Umm al-Kitāb—The Mother of the Book.
Al-Bukhārī, may Allah, the Exalted, have mercy upon him, said in his commentary on Sūrat al-Fātiḥah:
“It was named the Mother of the Book because the written copies of the Qur’an begin with it, and the recitation in prayer begins with it.”
It has also been called in transmitted reports:
The Treasure;
The Complete;
The Healer;
The Sufficient;
The Praise;
“All Praise Belongs to Allah”;
The Prayer;
The Cure;
The Foundation;
Gratitude;
and Supplication.
Al-Ḥāfiẓ Ibn Ḥajar mentioned these names in Fatḥ al-Bārī (8/106) and said:
“I gathered them from the transmitted reports.”

